 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><div class='qfig'><svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 320 110' width='320' height='110' role='img' aria-label='a metal spoon, a glass, a fabric sock and a wooden block'><g font-family='Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif'><ellipse cx='30.3' cy='30.3' rx='7.7' ry='11.1' fill='#d7dbe0' stroke='#6b7280' stroke-width='1.6' transform='rotate(45 30.3 30.3)'/><line x1='35.8' y1='35.8' x2='58.1' y2='58.1' stroke='#9aa0a6' stroke-width='4.173913043478261' stroke-linecap='round'/><text x='40.0' y='100.0' font-size='13' font-weight='700' fill='#2b2b2b' text-anchor='middle'>metal</text><rect x='101.9' y='21.9' width='36.2' height='36.2' rx='0' fill='#e9f5fb' stroke='#6aa7cf' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='110.3' y1='44.2' x2='124.2' y2='30.3' stroke='#ffffff' stroke-width='3' stroke-linecap='round'/><line x1='120.0' y1='21.9' x2='120.0' y2='58.1' stroke='#6aa7cf' stroke-width='2' stroke-linecap='round'/><line x1='101.9' y1='40.0' x2='138.1' y2='40.0' stroke='#6aa7cf' stroke-width='2' stroke-linecap='round'/><text x='120.0' y='100.0' font-size='13' font-weight='700' fill='#2b2b2b' text-anchor='middle'>glass</text><path d='M195.8 17.7 L208.3 17.7 L208.3 45.6 Q223.7 49.7 215.3 59.5 L195.8 55.3 Z' fill='#8e6bbf' stroke='#5a3f80' stroke-width='1.6'/><text x='200.0' y='100.0' font-size='13' font-weight='700' fill='#2b2b2b' text-anchor='middle'>fabric</text><rect x='264.7' y='24.7' width='30.6' height='30.6' rx='0' fill='#e2b77a' stroke='#8a5a2b' stroke-width='1.6'/><line x1='270.3' y1='34.4' x2='289.7' y2='34.4' stroke='#b98a52' stroke-width='1.4' stroke-linecap='round'/><line x1='270.3' y1='45.6' x2='289.7' y2='45.6' stroke='#b98a52' stroke-width='1.4' stroke-linecap='round'/><text x='280.0' y='100.0' font-size='13' font-weight='700' fill='#2b2b2b' text-anchor='middle'>wood</text></g></svg></div><p><b>Objects are made of materials.</b></p><ul><li>A spoon can be metal or plastic.</li><li>Glass is see-through.</li><li>Rubber is bendy; wool is soft.</li></ul><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>What is a window made of?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>you can see through it</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: glass</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Mixing up the object (a cup) with its material (plastic).</li><li>Thinking all shiny things are metal.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is a material?",
   "a": "A material is what an object is made of, such as wood, metal, plastic, glass, paper or fabric."
  },
  {
   "q": "What are properties?",
   "a": "Properties describe a material: hard or soft, rough or smooth, bendy or stiff, see-through or not."
  },
  {
   "q": "How can children test materials?",
   "a": "Drip water on them, shine a torch through them, bend them gently and feel them."
  }
 ],
